 tile. \n\nThis is really confusing. Given that, I think the correct action is to Pass, since forming a chow with B8 doesn't seem possible. \n\nTherefore, the answer is Pass.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The valid action \"Chi B8\" suggests forming a chow of [B7, B8, B9], but the player only holds B7 and B8, not B9. Since B9 is not in hand, this chow cannot be completed. Passing avoids an invalid move.  \nReason: The discarded tile B8 cannot form a valid chow with the current hand as B9 is missing.  \nAnswer: Pass"}
